      "final_chatbot_response": "A Gantt chart is a visual tool used to communicate the project schedule by displaying project activities against time. It shows start and finish dates, durations, overlap, dependencies, milestones, and progress. In your research project, a Gantt chart can help you organize and visualize the sequence of activities, identify dependencies between tasks, allocate time efficiently, track progress, and adjust the schedule when needed. It is recommended to build the Gantt chart from the Work Breakdown Structure (WBS) and update it when significant changes occur in the project timeline. By using a Gantt chart, you can effectively plan, monitor, and manage your research project to ensure timely completion and successful outcomes.",
